ES2024 added theMap.groupBy()method to JavaScript.

TheMap.groupBy()method groups the elements of an iterable according
to the values returned from a callback function.

TheMap.groupBy()method does not change the original object.

The return value is a Mapwith a key for each group, where each key is assigned to an Array of the associated elements.

Map.groupBy()is an ECMAScript 2024 feature.

JavaScript 2024is supported in new browsers sinceMarch 2024:

The difference between Object.groupBy() and Map.groupBy() is:

Object.groupBy() groups elements into a JavaScript object.

Map.groupBy() groups elements into a Map object.

